sbe1v1k: dts: fix the dtc warnings

dtc warns about this board:

  Warning (reg_format): /soc@0/mmc@7804000/card@0:reg: property has
    invalid length (4 bytes) (#address-cells == 2, #size-cells == 1)
  Warning (avoid_default_addr_size): .../card@0: Relying on default
    #address-cells / #size-cells value

and the failed reg_format check also disables the PCI checks, which
hid two more:

  Warning (pci_device_reg): /soc@0/pcie@18000000/pcie@0,0:reg: PCI reg
    config space address cells 2 and 3 must be 0
  Warning (pci_device_reg): /soc@0/pcie@20000000/pcie@0:reg: ...

 - &sdhc_1 gets #address-cells = <1> and #size-cells = <0> for its
   card@0 child, as in the MMC bindings.
 - The pcie2/pcie3 root port nodes had 1 and 2 in the low address cell
   of reg, apparently meant as a bus number. The root port is device 0,
   function 0 on bus 0 of its own domain, so reg is all zeros as on
   pcie1, and the pcie3 node is pcie@0 rather than pcie@0,0. Linux takes
   the devfn from the first reg cell only, which was 0 already, so the
   DT nodes still match the same root ports (and the wifi@0 nodes below
   them).

After this the board DTB builds without dtc warnings.

Same changes as OneNAS-space/Askey_Spectrum_SBE1V1K b6fc7b1f43.

Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
index baab57c524..b09811f4f4 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9570-sbe1v1k.dts
@@ -249,6 +249,9 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	status = "okay";
 
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
+
 	card@0 {
 		compatible = "mmc-card";
 		reg = <0>;
@@ -690,7 +693,7 @@
 
 	pcie@0 {
 		device_type = "pci";
-		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x1 0x0 0x0>;
+		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 		#address-cells = <3>;
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
@@ -743,9 +746,9 @@
 	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 33 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	status = "okay";
 
-	pcie@0,0 {
+	pcie@0 {
 		device_type = "pci";
-		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x2 0x0 0x0>;
+		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 		#address-cells = <3>;
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;
